  "findings": [
    {
      "level": "warn",
      "id": "version-drift",
      "lines": [
        "Version drift: appinfo/info.xml says 8.0.0, package.json says 8.0.0-dev.0, package-lock.json says 8.0.0-dev.0, package-lock.json packages[\"\"] says 8.0.0-dev.0.",
        "  make version of ncmake bumps info.xml, composer.json and package.json and re-syncs package-lock.json in one step, so they cannot drift apart. ncmake's lint-version workflow fails a push or a pull request on exactly this drift. The App Store and the server read info.xml, npm and composer read their own manifest. Whichever is behind, a release ends up carrying more than one version number, and only one of them reaches the user."
      ],
      "covers": [
        "lint-version/version-drift"
      ]
    },
    {
      "level": "warn",
      "id": "php-extensions",
      "lines": [
        "1 PHP extension is required by composer but not listed as <lib> in appinfo/info.xml:",
        "  exif (woltlab/webp-exif)",
        "  A Nextcloud server need not load it. The server checks <lib> before it enables the app; composer only checks where it runs. Without the <lib> the app is enabled anyway and the first call into the extension fails at runtime."
      ]
    },
    {
      "level": "info",
      "id": "node-version",
      "lines": [
        "Node stated as ^24.0.0 (package.json engines.node).",
        "  Not stated in .nvmrc, so nothing keeps the other places from drifting away from it.",
        "  The workflows read node-version from a variable, which is not resolved here, so whether CI builds on that major is not decidable from the checkout."
      ]
    },
    {
      "level": "info",
      "id": "tooling",
      "lines": [
        "Tooling in the checkout: ESLint (eslint.config.js), Stylelint (stylelint.config.cjs), Psalm (psalm.xml), PHPUnit (tests/phpunit.xml), PHP-CS-Fixer (.php-cs-fixer.dist.php), REUSE (REUSE.toml).",
        " No EditorConfig configuration: indentation is whatever each contributor's editor does."
      ]
    },
    {
      "level": "info",
      "id": "script-without-workflow",
      "lines": [
        "package.json declares the script ts:check, which no installed workflow runs.",
        "  The template lint-typescript of nextcloud/.github runs ts:check: make workflows-install W=lint-typescript",
        "  A check that no workflow runs on a pull request catches only what the contributor who remembers to run it catches."
      ]
    },
    {
      "level": "info",
      "id": "unreferenced-dependencies",
      "lines": [
        "10 declared packages are named nowhere in the checkout: @essentials/request-timeout, camelcase, path-posix, url-parse, vue-template-compiler, @vue/test-utils, dockerode, ts-node, and 2 more.",
        "  Searched as literal names over 808 files, package.json excluded apart from its non-dependency fields, lockfiles excluded; then as an ESLint shorthand, as what TypeScript takes from a tsconfig, and as a peer of an installed package in package-lock.json. A package loaded some other way is not named anywhere either, so this is a list to check, not a list to remove."
      ]
    },
    {
      "level": "info",
      "id": "license-drift",
      "lines": [
        "Licence agpl (appinfo/info.xml), AGPL-3.0-or-later (package.json), LICENSES/ holds AGPL-3.0-or-later.txt, Apache-2.0.txt, BSD-2-Clause.txt, BSD-3-Clause.txt, CC-BY-SA-4.0.txt, CC0-1.0.txt, GPL-3.0-or-later.txt, ISC.txt, MIT.txt, MPL-2.0.txt.",
        "  agpl in appinfo/info.xml is a deprecated App Store value, shown there as AGPLv3+, which is AGPL-3.0-or-later. With min-version 35 info.xml can state an SPDX id instead."
      ]
    },
    {
      "level": "ok",
      "id": "repository-link",
      "lines": [
        "appinfo/info.xml links its repository and its bug tracker."
      ]
    },
    {
